.TH GGE\-ASSETS 7 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
gge\-assets \- where files go and how they are loaded
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every path the engine takes is relative to
.IR <executable>/assets/ .
CMake copies the project's
.I assets/
folder next to the binary after each build, so edit files in the project and
rebuild.
.SS Layout
.nf
assets/sprites/   .png (ENGINE_WITH_IMAGE) or .bmp sheets
assets/tiles/     tilesets and Tiled .csv exports
assets/fonts/     .ttf (ENGINE_WITH_TTF)
assets/sfx/       .wav
assets/music/     .wav
.fi
.SS Loading
.BR assets_texture (3)
caches by path; call it freely in
.B on_enter
and never free the result.
.BR text_load_font (3)
returns a zero Font on failure, which draws with the debug font.
.BR audio_load (3)
returns a Sound the caller frees with
.BR audio_free (3)
in
.BR on_exit .
.BR tilemap_load_csv (3)
allocates; free with
.BR tilemap_free (3).
Failures log to the console and return NULL/false; nothing aborts, so run the
game from a terminal when something does not appear.
.SS Tilesets
One image, tiles left to right in rows, frame index = tile id. Keep frame 0
blank. 16 tiles across is a good width; families of variant tiles (autotile
masks, 9\-slices) go on their own rows so base indices are multiples of 16.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR assets_texture (3),
.BR assets_path (3),
